# A343131

For m >= 1, the m-digit number k = d_m||...||d_2||d_1 is a term if it is divisible by f_m(k) that is the sum of the m elementary symmetric polynomials in m variables e_i(k): f_m(k) = Sum_{i=1..m} e_i(d_1, ..., d_m).

The 62 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

